course: dictionary
lesson: 12197
title: Confines: the edges and limits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confines is a noun, and it is nearly always plural: we say the confines. It means the edges or limits of a place. Picture a fence around a field: the fence marks the confines of the field.
explain: «Pupils must stay within the confines of the playground.» The clue is stay within. The confines are the edges of the playground, so the children must keep inside them.
explain: The word can also mean the limits of an idea, rule or activity. «They worked within the confines of the law.» Here the confines are the lines the law sets, the limits you must not cross. In stories, a character who longs to escape the confines of a small room wants to get out past its walls.
explain: Watch for the phrases that often come with it: within the confines of, beyond the confines of, and the narrow confines of. «Beyond the confines of» means past the limit. «The narrow confines» means a small, tight space.
fact: Confines means the edges or limits of a place.
fact: Confines can also mean the limits of an idea, rule or activity.
fact: Confines is nearly always used in the plural, as the confines.
fact: «Within the confines of» means inside the limits of something.
fact: «Beyond the confines of» means past the limits of something.
exercise: «Pupils must stay within the confines of the playground.» What are the confines here? | The games the children like best | The bell that rings at break time | The tall trees growing near the gate | *The edges and limits of the playground
exercise: «They worked within the confines of the law.» What does confines mean in this sentence? | *The limits that the law sets | The lawyers who work in the town | The lights in the court room | A long, slow walk
exercise: Which phrase means past the limits of something? | *beyond the confines of | a kind of tree | within the confines of | the narrow confines
test: «She longed to escape the confines of her small room.» What does this suggest? | *She wants to get out past its walls | She is happy to stay there forever | She has just moved into a bigger house | She is painting the room blue
test: Find the word that means the edges or limits of a place or rule. | conifer | *confines | confetti | confident
exam: «Within the confines of the park, dogs must stay on a lead.» What does within the confines of the park mean? | Far away from the park gates | *Inside the edges and limits of the park | Dressed up for the park party | Under the park benches
